## Part 1 — correct the `Add` operator

**File:** `services/calc/calc.go`

**Contract.** `Add(a, b int) int` returns the integer sum of its two arguments.
It is a pure total function: no state, no I/O, no error path, no panics, and
order-independent (`Add(a, b) == Add(b, a)`). Keep the exported name,
the parameter list `(a, b int)`, the single `int` result and the `package calc`
declaration exactly as they are — the test file calls `calc.Add` with that
signature, so any change to the name, arity, parameter types or return type
would break compilation of a file the writer is forbidden to edit.

**Intended implementation.** Replace the body's subtraction with addition, so
the function returns the sum of `a` and `b` rather than their difference. This
is a one-expression change to the existing single-line function body; keep the
file otherwise byte-identical (same package clause, no new imports, no added
helpers, no extra exported symbols). Do not introduce a wrapper, an interface,
a configuration flag, or a second code path — the spec describes one plain
arithmetic function and the tests exercise it directly.

**Tests this part serves.** Both tests in the failing set, and nothing else is
needed to close the set:

